    "value": "8"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1984-p16.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The relation shows that every root \\(2+r\\) is paired with \\(2-r.\\) Four distinct roots therefore form two such pairs, and each pair has sum \\(4.\\) The sum of all four roots is \\(2\\cdot4=8.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "The equation makes the graph symmetric about \\(x=2\\)",
        "Pair each root \\(2+r\\) with its reflected root \\(2-r\\)"
      ],
